Hi,

recently my AXPpci33, running Tru64, started forgetting it's SRM-
Settings. It's now in a state that upon every Power-Cycle it has console 
set to "serial" instead of "graphics", "os_type" set to "OpenVMS" 
instead of "UNIX" (and probably more).

Now, I also keep getting alerts from Tru64 telling me that the TOY-
Battery was low. And in SRC the date displayed is weird.

So I checked the AXPpci33 and found a DS1287 and a DS1225AD-150. I 
think, batteries in both are empty.

While the DS1225AD-150 is still available I'm not sure about the DS1287. 
I found a note on the Maxim-Site that in MOST cases the SD1287 can be 
replaced by a DS12887 but that there might be Problems accessing the 
correct Address Partition :-(

Now, before ordering a DS12887 and then regret when it does not work I 
thought I'd ask here:

Does anybody know if the DS12887+ will work as a replacement for the 
DS1287 on the AXPpci33?

If it's definitely not compatible I'd go the "add an external Battery to 
DS1287" way - but I'd prefer to replace the DS1287.

If there's no experience I'll give the DS12887+ a try and report if it 
worked...

Btw: Is there any Info in the DS1287 or DS1225AD that might/will cause 
Problems if these get replaced, like in the SparcStation 10 (fortunately 
I was prepared for the Battery to run empty)?

MTIA and Cheers,
_ralf_


